{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"atomic operations atomic operations","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md","fileName":"Atomic Operations.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Atomic Operations","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony]] [[.NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony",".NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"atomic operations atomic operations","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md","fileName":"Atomic Operations.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Atomic Operations","heading":"Atomic Operations","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An atomic operation appears indivisible to competing threads: no observer sees it half-complete. .NET's `Interlocked` operations provide atomic increments, exchanges, additions, and compare-and-swap behavior for selected primitive locations.\n\nAtomic primitives avoid a full lock for small state transitions, but they do not automatically protect a larger invariant spanning several values. Correct lock-free design requires the entire algorithm, not just one assignment, to remain valid under every interleaving.\n\nInterlocked operations also establish the memory-order boundary required for other threads to observe the transition consistently. That ordering guarantee is part of their synchronization role, not merely a faster spelling of arithmetic.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony",".NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"atomic operations atomic operations","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Atomic Operations.md","fileName":"Atomic Operations.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Atomic Operations","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n[[hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony",".NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}